ShapeFix: the repair of a wire's non-adjacent intersecting edges
(ShapeFix_IntersectionTool::FixSelfIntersectWire, run for each wire of a
face by ShapeFix_Wire::FixSelfIntersection) applied the context to the whole
face (ShapeBuild_ReShape::Apply) and went through all the vertices of the
face for their largest tolerance, once for each wire: quadratic in the wires
of a face (a face with thousands of holes). The face is applied with
ShapeBuild_ReShape::ApplyAgain, which returns the result and the status of
the previous call for the same shape when no request has been recorded or
cleared since and that call recorded none itself (Apply would find the same
requests in the same shape and rebuild nothing); ShapeBuild_ReShape counts
the requests for it (replace, Clear). The largest tolerance is found only
for a wire with two edges that may intersect, before anything is changed,
so it is the same value. The repair of intersecting wires of a face
(FixIntersectingWires) made the edge list of the second wire of every pair
of wires before the test of their boxes; it is made only for the pairs whose
boxes meet. The results, the requests recorded and the statuses are
unchanged. ShapeBuild_ReShape gets members (code built against the port's
headers must be rebuilt with them).
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeBuild/ShapeBuild_ReShape.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeBuild/ShapeBuild_ReShape.cxx
index dc170a79..a4787b08 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeBuild/ShapeBuild_ReShape.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeBuild/ShapeBuild_ReShape.cxx
@@ -337,3 +337,62 @@ bool ShapeBuild_ReShape::Status(const ShapeExtend_Status theStatus) const
 {
   return ShapeExtend::DecodeStatus(myStatus, theStatus);
 }
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+void ShapeBuild_ReShape::Clear()
+{
+  ++myNbChanges;
+  BRepTools_ReShape::Clear();
+}
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+void ShapeBuild_ReShape::replace(const TopoDS_Shape&    theShape,
+                                 const TopoDS_Shape&    theNewShape,
+                                 const TReplacementKind theKind)
+{
+  ++myNbChanges;
+  BRepTools_ReShape::replace(theShape, theNewShape, theKind);
+}
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+TopoDS_Shape ShapeBuild_ReShape::ApplyAgain(const TopoDS_Shape& theShape)
+{
+  if (DynamicType() != STANDARD_TYPE(ShapeBuild_ReShape))
+  {
+    // a derived class may find or apply its requests otherwise
+    return Apply(theShape);
+  }
+
+  // The result of Apply depends on the requests (unchanged since the last call
+  // here if none has been recorded or cleared), the mode of locations and the
+  // shape. A call that recorded no request rebuilt nothing: it would give the
+  // same result and status again.
+  const bool aConsiderLocation = ModeConsiderLocation();
+  if (myHasAgain && myAgainNbChanges == myNbChanges
+      && myAgainConsiderLocation == aConsiderLocation && myAgainShape.IsEqual(theShape))
+  {
+    myStatus = myAgainStatus;
+    return myAgainResult;
+  }
+
+  const size_t       aNbChanges = myNbChanges;
+  const TopoDS_Shape aResult    = Apply(theShape);
+  myHasAgain                    = (myNbChanges == aNbChanges);
+  if (myHasAgain)
+  {
+    myAgainShape            = theShape;
+    myAgainResult           = aResult;
+    myAgainStatus           = myStatus;
+    myAgainNbChanges        = myNbChanges;
+    myAgainConsiderLocation = aConsiderLocation;
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    myAgainShape.Nullify();
+    myAgainResult.Nullify();
+  }
+  return aResult;
+}
